From: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
Date: Thu, 21 Aug 2025 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: swphy: accept 10G fixed-link speed

The Mono Gateway's 10G MACs (xfi) use a fixed-link at 10000 Mbit/s. mainline's
swphy only decodes 10/100/1000, so a 10G fixed-link returns -EINVAL and the MAC
fails to probe ("swphy: unknown speed"). Decode 10000 like 1000 (the swphy MII
register set has no distinct 10G code), matching the NXP LSDK kernel.

Signed-off-by: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
---
--- a/drivers/net/phy/swphy.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/swphy.c
@@ -71,6 +71,7 @@
 static int swphy_decode_speed(int speed)
 {
 	switch (speed) {
+	case 10000:
 	case 1000:
 		return SWMII_SPEED_1000;
 	case 100:
